  "body": "> If a reflecting IDL attribute is a DOMString or USVString attribute but doesn't fall into any of the above categories, then the getting and setting must be done in a transparent, case-preserving manner.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't appear to cover what the getter should return when the attribute is not present.\r\n\r\nSome testing of `textarea.wrap` and `marquee.direction` reveals it should return the empty string. But we should be explicit.",
